<title>HUNGARY: Hungary's hog numbers rise to 5.8 million.</title>
<headline>Hungary's hog numbers rise to 5.8 million.</headline>
<dateline>BUDAPEST 1996-09-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>Hungary's hog numbers rose to 5.80 million as at August 1, up 14 percent from their June 30, 1995 level, the Central Statistical Office (KSH) said in a statement.</p>
<p>The number of sows reached 426,000, up three percent.</p>
<p>No KSH official was immediately available to explain why KSH compared the August 1 data with end-June last year.</p>
<p>&quot;The situation of pig breeders continued to deteriorate in the reviewed period,&quot; KSH said, adding that individual breeders suffered the biggest falls in profitability. @</p>
<p>&quot;This will presumably induce an increase in meat prices in the coming one year period,&quot; it said. --Budapest newsroom (36 1) 327-4040</p>
</text>
